/ The mark keeps half its width from each end, so it stays inside. The
  period of an end stands below its number, at the same side. A sheet lists
  the ends with their links instead, so it leaves out the periods.
span class='flex w-full flex-col gap-1.5'
  span class='relative block h-1 w-full rounded-full bg-fill-strong' aria-hidden='true'
    span class='absolute -top-1 w-1 h-3 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-sm bg-fg ring-2 ring-surface' style="left: clamp(0.125rem, #{position}%, 100% - 0.125rem)"
  span class='flex justify-between gap-4 text-xs leading-tight tabular-nums text-muted'
    - ends.each do |number, period|
      span class='flex flex-col last:text-right'
        span.font-semibold.text-fg-secondary = number
        span.tooltip-hover-only = period
